### OneClick Backend — IntelliJ HTTP Client tests
###
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  Setup
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###
### 1. Lance Spring : Run config "OneClick (oauth2)" → ▶
### 2. Régénère les JWT (durée 1h) :
###       ./scripts/regen-jwt-env.sh
###    Ce script écrit 4 JWT signés (admin/client/restaurateur/tenant_admin)
###    dans http-client.private.env.json (gitignored).
### 3. Sélecteur d'environnement (top right de ce fichier) → "oauth2"
### 4. Clique le ▶ vert à côté de chaque ###.
###
### Si une requête retourne 401, ton JWT a expiré → re-lance regen-jwt-env.sh.
###
### Variables disponibles dans {{ }} :
###   {{base}}                URL base (http://localhost:8081)
###   {{jwtAdmin}}            JWT signé pour un user admin
###   {{jwtClient}}           JWT signé pour un user client
###   {{jwtRestaurateur}}     JWT signé pour un user restaurateur
###   {{jwtTenantAdmin}}      JWT signé pour un user tenant_admin
###   {{adminUserId}}         UUID de l'admin (utile dans des PATCH ciblés)

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 1. Health & infra (publics — pas de JWT requis)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Health check
GET {{base}}/actuator/health

### Info build/git
GET {{base}}/actuator/info

### OpenAPI 3 spec (pour générer un client SDK ailleurs)
GET {{base}}/v3/api-docs

### Swagger UI (URL — ouvre dans le navigateur, pas dans le HTTP Client)
GET {{base}}/swagger-ui/index.html

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 2. Sécurité — sans JWT, on doit avoir 401
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Pas de header Authorization → 401
GET {{base}}/api/tenants

### JWT bidon → 401 (signature invalide)
GET {{base}}/api/tenants
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ0ZXN0In0.fake-signature

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 3. Endpoints sécurisés — JWT admin
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Liste des tenants (admin only)
GET {{base}}/api/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### Tenant par slug
GET {{base}}/api/tenants/by-slug/palmeraie
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### Liste paginée des restaurants à Casablanca (vue read-only optimisée)
GET {{base}}/api/restaurants/core/by-city?city=Casablanca&page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### Détail d'un restaurant complet (33 colonnes — JSONB opening_hours visible)
GET {{base}}/api/restaurants/8ad6e68c-2a69-496d-b9b0-33110c4722ce
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### Réservations par status "demandée" (note l'URL-encoding %C3%A9 = é)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/by-status?status=demand%C3%A9e
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### Loyalty points (FIFO système)
GET {{base}}/api/loyalty-points
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### Notifications in-app (40k+ rows)
GET {{base}}/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### Bookable resources PCC (Padel/Spa/Golf)
GET {{base}}/api/bookable-resources
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### Vue audit log (read-only @Immutable)
GET {{base}}/api/views/admin-audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 4. Permissions par rôle (Phase 6.2)
###    Voir comment le filtre @PreAuthorize + @RequirePermission applique
###    différents accès selon le JWT utilisé.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### admin → /api/tenants → 200 (admin a tenant.READ)
GET {{base}}/api/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### client → /api/tenants → 403 (client n'a PAS tenant.READ)
###   Body : ProblemDetails RFC 7807 avec traceId
GET {{base}}/api/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtClient}}

### restaurateur → /api/admin-audit-logs → 403 (admin only)
GET {{base}}/api/admin-audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtRestaurateur}}

### admin → /api/admin-audit-logs → 200
GET {{base}}/api/admin-audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### client → /api/restaurants/core/by-city → 200 (client a restaurant.READ)
GET {{base}}/api/restaurants/core/by-city?city=Casablanca&size=2
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtClient}}

### client → /api/partner-contracts → 403 (admin only)
GET {{base}}/api/partner-contracts
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtClient}}

### restaurateur → /api/loyalty-points → 200
GET {{base}}/api/loyalty-points
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtRestaurateur}}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 5. Recherche dynamique (Phase 6.3)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Recherche : profils dont prénom commence par "You"
POST {{base}}/api/profiles/search
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "criteria": [
    {"field": "firstName", "op": "ILIKE", "value": "You%"}
  ],
  "size": 5
}

### Recherche combinée : prénom ILIKE + score GTE + tri desc
POST {{base}}/api/profiles/search
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "criteria": [
    {"field": "firstName", "op": "ILIKE", "value": "You%"},
    {"field": "reliabilityScore", "op": "GTE", "value": 3.5}
  ],
  "sort": "reliabilityScore,desc",
  "page": 0,
  "size": 10
}

### Recherche IN sur city
POST {{base}}/api/profiles/search
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "criteria": [
    {"field": "city", "op": "IN", "value": ["Casablanca", "Marrakech", "Rabat"]}
  ],
  "size": 5
}

### Recherche IS_NOT_NULL sur reliabilityScore
POST {{base}}/api/profiles/search
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "criteria": [
    {"field": "reliabilityScore", "op": "IS_NOT_NULL", "value": null}
  ],
  "sort": "reliabilityScore,desc",
  "size": 5
}

### Tentative avec field non whitelisté → 400 + ProblemDetails RFC 7807
###   Body retourné liste les champs autorisés
POST {{base}}/api/profiles/search
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "criteria": [
    {"field": "internalSecret", "op": "EQ", "value": "x"}
  ]
}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 6. Validation Bean (Phase 6.1) + Exception handler RFC 7807 (Phase 5.0)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Profil par UUID inexistant → 404 + ProblemDetails not-found
GET {{base}}/api/profiles/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### UUID malformé → 400 + ProblemDetails type-mismatch
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/not-a-valid-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### PATCH valide → 200 + entité modifiée + log [AUDIT] côté Spring
PATCH {{base}}/api/profiles/{{adminUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "city": "Tanger",
  "language": "fr"
}

### PATCH avec phone format invalid → 400 + fieldErrors
PATCH {{base}}/api/profiles/{{adminUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "INVALID-PHONE!!"
}

### Route inexistante → 404 + ProblemDetails route-not-found
GET {{base}}/api/foo-bar-baz
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

### Missing query param → 400 + ProblemDetails missing-parameter
GET {{base}}/api/user-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtAdmin}}

